  "body": "Stacked on #2985 (merge #2985 first). This PR has one commit of its own on top of the #2985 head `73e10f954`: `7e6e2ffe3`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The first-traverse law (#2985) now reads the machine table on a 3+2 plane. Before, it skipped the table in each tilted frame.\n- The law reads the table's top face over the stated X/Y travel. The table box is clipped to the Z travel, which starts at the table top. The 1e6 mm slab under the top face is out of the tool's reach.\n- The law reads the table only when the head can tilt. The machine file states which rotaries turn the work (`turns_part`, #804). When each tilting rotary turns the work, the table stays under the work, and the law does not read the table.\n- A mounted machine that states no X, Y and Z travel has no table box. A 3+2 plane on such a machine gets a note: \"First traverse: the machine table is not judged on this tilted plane: ...\". It is not a silent pass.\n- Files: `crates/app/src/operation/first_traverse.rs` (the predicate `work_tilts`, the clip `table_top_face`, the note), and `generate.rs` (passes the rotary list, adds the note to the path).\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2987-table-tilted-first-traverse.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\n- #2985 skipped the table in a tilted frame. A full read of the table box refused each indexed operation on the microARC 4.\n- I measured why. A read of the top face alone still refused them: Z 190.5 at A 90 and Z 336.55 at A 180. Those refusals are false. The microARC 4 turns the work, so its table never stands over the plane.\n- On a head-tilt machine the table is fixed in the world. The tilted plane drops toward it on its low side. That collision passed.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew file `crates/app/tests/first_traverse_table.rs`. It uses a small test machine (X and Y travel +-100 mm, Z travel 0..300 mm) with three rigs: head tilt, work tilt, and head tilt with no travel.\n\n- `a_head_tilt_plane_under_the_table_inside_the_travel_is_refused_by_name`: B 30 deg, plane 20 mm over the origin, table top face at 32.68 mm along the axis. The verdict is `FirstTraverseLow { fixture: true }` and the post is refused by name. **Red before the fix.**\n- `a_head_tilt_machine_with_no_travel_names_the_table_unjudged`: the note is on the path. **Red before the fix.**\n- `a_head_tilt_past_90_reads_the_table_top_face_not_its_slab`: B 120 deg. A plane 100 mm over the origin passes, and a plane 90 mm over it is refused at the top face (96.6 mm).\n- `a_head_tilt_plane_over_the_table_top_face_passes`: control.\n- `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work`: control, the same plane as the refused case.\n\nMutation checks (each run, then restored):\n- The old `first_traverse.rs` and `generate.rs` from #2985: the refusal pin and the note pin fail.\n- No top-face clip (the full slab): `a_head_tilt_past_90_reads_the_table_top_face_not_its_slab` fails.\n- `work_turns = false`: `a_work_turning_rotary_keeps_the_table_under_the_work` fails.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base base-2985` (the #2985 head; my diff only): 116 steps, 0 failed.\n- These suites passed separately (45 binaries): `first_4axis_part`, `fourth_axis_pose`, `index_swing`, `index_swing_horizontal`, `tilt`, `tilt_a180`, `tilt_a180_routes`, `tilt_heights`, `tilt_basis_compat`, `stock_source_holes`, `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `continuous_4axis_part`, `first_router_part`, `tormach_fourth_axis`, the `wcs_*` suites and others.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes. The indexed example operations that posted on #2985 still post.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- App heavy lanes: the [reviewer ran `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2997#issuecomment-7045080077) on this head trial-merged with main at `97a880c53`: 199 steps, 198 ok, 1 failed (`pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean`). The reviewer reproduced the same failure with main's `first_traverse.rs` and `generate.rs`, so the failure is not from this PR.\n- No machine run.\n- The law runs at generation only (as in #2985). If the user loads a different machine after a generate, the first traverse is not judged again until the next generate. This gap is in #2985's design and also applies to the fixtures.\n- A machine with a head tilt and a vertical work C: the table footprint is read without the C turn.\n- An old project whose rotary has no `turns_part` is read as a head tilt (the conservative reading). It can be refused where it posted on #2985.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- Stacked on #2985: the same function `operation::first_traverse::judge` and the `Over` struct. #2985 adds the file.\n- No other open PR changes these files.\n\nChangelog: The first rapid of a 3+2 operation on a head-tilt machine is now refused by name when its clearance plane goes under the machine table top inside the machine travel; a machine that states no travel gets a note that the table was not judged.\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #2985\n\nFixes #2987\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
